Phase OS-18: Kernel Device Driver Enhancements - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/dev_usb.asm (USB Device Management)
   - Base ID: 916
   - USB device enumeration, configuration, and data transfer management
   - Features: USB device enumeration, endpoint configuration, bulk/interrupt/control transfers, device descriptor parsing, power management, USB hub support
   - Data structures: usb_device_t (dev_addr, vendor_id, product_id, num_endpoints, speed, state), usb_endpoint_t (ep_addr, ep_type, max_packet, direction)
   - API: dev_usb_init, dev_usb_enumerate, dev_usb_get_device(index), dev_usb_config_ep(dev_addr, ep), dev_usb_bulk_transfer(dev_addr, ep, buf, len), dev_usb_control_transfer(dev_addr, request, value, buf, len), dev_usb_disconnect(dev_addr)
   - Capacity: 32 USB devices, 128 endpoints, 4 transfer types (control, bulk, interrupt, isochronous)
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/dev_i2c.asm (I2C Bus Controller)
   - Base ID: 917
   - I2C (Inter-Integrated Circuit) bus master/slave communication
   - Features: I2C bus initialization, master transmit/receive, clock speed configuration (100kHz/400kHz/3.4MHz), address scanning, multi-byte transfers, ACK/NACK handling
   - Data structures: i2c_bus_t (bus_id, speed_hz, num_devices, error_count), i2c_transfer_t (addr, buf, len, direction, status)
   - API: dev_i2c_init(bus_id, speed_hz), dev_i2c_write(bus_id, addr, buf, len), dev_i2c_read(bus_id, addr, buf, len), dev_i2c_write_reg(bus_id, addr, reg, val), dev_i2c_read_reg(bus_id, addr, reg), dev_i2c_scan(bus_id, out_devices), dev_i2c_stats(bus_id, out_stats)
   - Capacity: 4 I2C buses, 128 devices per bus, 3 speed modes
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

3. kernel/dev_spi.asm (SPI Bus Controller)
   - Base ID: 918
   - SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface) bus master communication
   - Features: SPI bus initialization, full-duplex transfer, clock polarity/phase (CPOL/CPHA) configuration, chip select management, DMA-ready transfers, multiple slave devices
   - Data structures: spi_bus_t (bus_id, speed_hz, cpol, cpha, num_slaves), spi_transfer_t (cs_line, tx_buf, rx_buf, len, status)
   - API: dev_spi_init(bus_id, speed_hz, cpol, cpha), dev_spi_transfer(bus_id, cs, tx_buf, rx_buf, len), dev_spi_write(bus_id, cs, buf, len), dev_spi_read(bus_id, cs, buf, len), dev_spi_set_cs(bus_id, cs, active), dev_spi_stats(bus_id, out_stats)
   - Capacity: 4 SPI buses, 8 chip select lines per bus, 4 clock modes
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

